{"id": "SGU_Episode_668", "title": "SGU Episode 668", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 668 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 668", "date": "April 28 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 4, "day": 28, "rogues": ["Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella", "Cara Santa Maria"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Asimov", "quote": "\n Anti-intellectualism has been a constant thread winding its way through our political and cultural life, nurtured by the false idea that democracy means \"my ignorance is just as good as your knowledge.\" \n", "quotee": "\n Isaac Asimov ", "quotee_title": " American writer\n", "guests": [{"guest": "Tobias F\u00fcchslin", "guest_title": "research manager at Media Pulse", "guest_url": "https://twitter.com/tofu89"}], "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-668", "episode_number": 668}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "Voice-over: You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction, sicknesses, SGU's sound editing", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction, sicknesses, SGU's sound editing"}, "sections": [{"id": 1, "text": "...bent[v 1]", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "J", "speaker": "Jay Novella"}}]}, {"id": 2, "text": "Annealing[v 2]", "title": "What's the Word?", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:11:38", "hour": 0, "minute": "11", "second": "38", "title": "What's the Word?"}, "sections": [{"id": 3, "text": "W\u0113t\u0101\n", "title": "W\u0113t\u0101 Workshop, sword making, metallurgy", "metadata": {"title": "W\u0113t\u0101 Workshop, sword making, metallurgy"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 4, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 5, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 6, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 7, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "C", "speaker": "Cara Santa Maria"}}, {"id": 8, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "J", "speaker": "Jay Novella"}}, {"id": 9, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 10, "text": "(laughs)\n(laughter)\n(applause)\n[inaudible]", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 11, "text": "\nThe myth of the online echo chamber\u00a0[2]\n\n\n", "title": "Are Echochambers a Myth?", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:23:33", "hour": 0, "minute": "23", "second": "33", "links": ["https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20180416-the-myth-of-the-online-echo-chamber"], "title": "Are Echochambers a Myth?"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 12, "text": "\nOrganic solar cells reach record efficiency, benchmark for commercialization\u00a0[1]\u00a0\n\n\n", "title": "Organic Solar Cells", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:42:37", "hour": 0, "minute": "42", "second": "37", "links": ["https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2018/04/180423110813.htm"], "title": "Organic Solar Cells"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 13, "text": "\nHow science made a self-cleaning coating that repels all liquid\u00a0[3]\n\n\n", "title": "Self-Cleaning Coating", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:51:52", "hour": 0, "minute": "51", "second": "52", "links": ["https://www.theverge.com/2018/4/16/17243600/self-cleaning-phone-screen-anish-tuteja-materials-repellent"], "title": "Self-Cleaning Coating"}, "sections": [{"id": 14, "text": "...\"Nearly-Headless Nick\"...", "metadata": {"links": ["https://harrypotter.fandom.com/wiki/Nicholas_de_Mimsy-Porpington"], "speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}]}]}, {"id": 15, "text": "", "title": "Who's That Noisy?", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:58:50", "hour": 0, "minute": "58", "second": "50", "title": "Who's That Noisy?"}, "sections": [{"id": 16, "text": "[creaking and winding noises]\n\nwhat this noisy is\n", "title": "New Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:02:18", "hour": "1", "minute": "02", "second": "18", "title": "New Noisy"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 17, "text": "Tobias F\u00fcchslin, Research Manager Online at Media Pulse (in Switzerland)\n\"Probability and conspiratorial thinking\", by Marko Kovic and Tobias F\u00fcchslin", "title": "Interview with Tobias F\u00fcchslin", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:02:51", "hour": "1", "minute": "02", "second": "51", "links": ["https://twitter.com/tofu89", "http://mediapulse.ch", "https://osf.io/preprints/socarxiv/b6qtf/"], "title": "Interview with Tobias F\u00fcchslin"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 18, "text": "Voice-over: It's time for Science or Fiction.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:16:51", "hour": "1", "minute": "16", "second": "51", "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": [{"id": 19, "text": "", "title": "Jay's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Jay's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 20, "text": "", "title": "Evan's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Evan's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 21, "text": "", "title": "Cara's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Cara's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 22, "text": "", "title": "Bob's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Bob's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 23, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #1", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #1"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 24, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #2", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #2"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 25, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #3", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #3"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 26, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:41:39", "hour": "1", "minute": "41", "second": "39", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 27, "text": "", "title": "Signoff", "metadata": {"title": "Signoff"}, "sections": [{"id": 28, "text": "\u2014and until next week, this is your  Skeptics' Guide to the Universe.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 29, "text": "Skeptics' Guide to the Universe is produced by SGU Productions, dedicated to promoting science and critical thinking. For more information, visit us at theskepticsguide.org. Send your questions to info@theskepticsguide.org. And, if you would like to support the show and all the work that we do, go to patreon.com/SkepticsGuide and consider becoming a patron and becoming part of the SGU community. Our listeners and supporters are what make SGU possible.", "metadata": {"links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org", "https://www.patreon.com/SkepticsGuide"], "speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}]}, {"id": 30, "text": "", "title": "Today I Learned", "metadata": {"title": "Today I Learned"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 31, "text": "\n\u2191 1.0 1.1 University of Michigan: Organic solar cells reach record efficiency, benchmark for commercialization\n\n\u2191 BBC Future: The myth of the online echo chamber\n\n\u2191 The Verge: How science made a self-cleaning coating that repels all liquid\n\n\u2191 Frontiers:\u00a0Metabolic and Fatigue Profiles are Comparable Between Prepubertal Children and Well-Trained Adult Endurance Athletes\n\n\u2191 YaleNews:\u00a0Study shows newspaper op-eds change minds\n\n\u2191 ScienceDaily:\u00a0Einstein's 'spooky action' goes massive\n\n\u2191 [url_for_TIL publication: title]\n\n", "title": "References", "metadata": {"links": ["https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2018/04/180423110813.htm", "https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20180416-the-myth-of-the-online-echo-chamber", "https://www.theverge.com/2018/4/16/17243600/self-cleaning-phone-screen-anish-tuteja-materials-repellent", "https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2018.00387/full", "https://news.yale.edu/2018/04/24/study-shows-newspaper-op-eds-change-minds", "https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2018/04/180425131858.htm"], "title": "References"}, "sections": [{"id": 32, "text": "\n\u2191 Wiktionary: bend (to apply to a task or purpose)\n\n\u2191 Wiktionary: annealing\n\n", "title": "Vocabulary", "metadata": {"links": ["https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bend#Verb", "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/annealing"], "title": "Vocabulary"}, "sections": []}]}]}